<title>FRANCE: French centre-right holds lead in election -poll.</title>
<headline>French centre-right holds lead in election -poll.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the results of an opinion poll of voters' intentions ahead of the May 25/June 1 parlimentary election.</p>
<p>The telephone poll of 1,633 adults aged 18 and over was conducted by IPSOS on May 13 and 14 for the Le Point weekly newsmagazine to be appear on May 17.</p>
<p>			   percentage  projected seats in</p>
<p>			    of vote    National Assembly</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Extreme left	     1.5	     na</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Communists		 9.0	     27</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Socialists-other left  28.5	   226</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Ecologists		  5.5	    na</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> RPR/UDF-other right    39.0	   323</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> National Front	   15.0	     1</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p>NOTE: Ipsos said 57 percent of those polled said they were very sure they would vote as projected and 43 percent could still change their minds. 26 percent did not express a voting intention. The poll covered all the 577 seats in France including the 22 seats in overseas territories.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
